{{- /*
  support/whats-next-mapping — the shared "state → what's next phrase"
  Markdown table used verbatim in the summary sections of the two
  list-level sweep prompts (Support: watch channel and Support:
  housekeeping). Both callers render the same 6-row core table
  (`triaged`, `gathering-info`, `need-info`, `drafting`,
  `awaiting-customer`, `awaiting-us`); watch-channel additionally
  prints two closing-state rows (`resolved`, `stale`).

  Fields on the `dict` argument:

    IncludeClosed:  when true, appends the two closing-state rows
                    (`resolved` and `stale`). Watch-channel sets this
                    true; housekeeping does not surface closing rows
                    in its what's-next table (they've been removed
                    from the open backlog in Step 4).

  Usage — the caller supplies the surrounding bullet + preamble text
  and drops the fragment where the table body goes; both callers
  render the table at 4-space indent (nested inside their bullet), so
  the fragment emits its rows at 4-space indent as well:

      - **Always end with a "what's next" table** listing every ticket ...
        (prompt-specific preamble sentences here)

        {{ template "_shared/support/whats-next-mapping" (dict "IncludeClosed" false) }}

        **The "What's next" cell must be a markdown link ...

  Whitespace: fragment body starts and ends flush (no leading/trailing
  newline); the surrounding YAML newlines and the caller's indent
  provide framing. Every rendered line is indented 4 spaces so the
  table lines up under a bullet.
*/ -}}
{{- $includeClosed := .IncludeClosed -}}
| state | what's next |
  |-------|-------------|
  | `triaged` | Needs investigation |
  | `gathering-info` | Investigation in progress |
  | `need-info` | Needs more info from user |
  | `drafting` | Ready to reply to user |
  | `awaiting-customer` | Waiting on customer reply |
  | `awaiting-us` | Our turn — needs a response |
{{- if $includeClosed }}
  | `resolved` | Resolved (closing) |
  | `stale` | Stale — auto-closing |
{{- end }}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
